In all the processes listed above, a proton–hydride coupling (Eq. 1) is formally responsible for the release of H2.

In addition to these systems, ‘destabilized hydrides’ have also been recently developed, which release H2 by

\begin{equation}
2\ MgH_2+Si\rightarrow Mg_2Si+2\ H_2\left(\Delta H^0=+0.38\ eV\right)
\end{equation}

\begin{equation}
2\mathrm{LiBH_{4}+MgH_{2}\rightarrow2LiH+MgB_{2}+4H_{2}(\Delta H^{0}=+0.42\ eV)}
\end{equation}

\begin{token}
